# ── easystock-frontend runtime env ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Almost every var the frontend reads is `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, baked into the image AT
# BUILD TIME (§10.1) — listed below, and NOT read from this file. The running
# container reads only what is in this first block, via docker-compose's
# `env_file: ./.env.frontend`. Copy it to /opt/easystock/{production,staging}/.env.frontend.
NODE_ENV=production

# Server-only secret, read at RUNTIME (never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never in the browser).
# Every server-side render / proxy lookup sends it so the backend's global per-IP
# rate limiter skips this server — it renders every shop from ONE IP, and without
# it all shoppers of all stores share one bucket (shops 404 / custom domains
# redirect to /login when it runs dry; 2026-10-23).
# MUST equal SSR_API_KEY in .env.backend of the same environment. 32+ chars,
# e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Empty = no exemption. Changing it needs only a
# container restart, no rebuild. Separate values for production and staging.
SSR_API_KEY=

# ── BUILD-TIME vars (NOT read here — listed so this stays the env registry) ────
# Set as `build-args` in inventory-frontend/.github/workflows/deploy.yml, declared
# as ARG/ENV in its Dockerfile. Editing this file does NOT change a running
# container: changing any of them requires a REBUILD + redeploy of the image.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL
#     Backend API base, including /api. Per environment:
#       production →  https://api.ezycore.com/api
#       staging    →  https://rc-api.ezycore.com/api
#     Supplied from the repo secrets NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL_PROD / _STAGING.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN
#     Apex domain workspaces live under; builds per-workspace subdomain URLs
#     (acme.ezycore.com). production → ezycore.com, staging → "" (empty).
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STOREFRONT_ROOT_DOMAIN
#     Tenant root domain for the storefront; MUST match NEXT_PUBLIC_ROOT_DOMAIN.
#     Subdomains (rmc.ezycore.com) are parsed as store slugs against this value.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_CUSTOM_DOMAIN_MAP
#     Manual override, custom domain → store slug as JSON: {"mystore.com":"rmc41"}.
#     Normally unneeded — self-serve domains resolve dynamically via
#     /api/public/store-by-host in proxy.ts. The Dockerfile declares the ARG but
#     deploy.yml does not pass it, so it is empty in every built image today.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GIT_SHA
#     The commit the image was built from, shown beside the release in the user
#     menu. deploy.yml passes `github.sha`; nothing to set by hand.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION
#     Not a build arg: next.config.mjs reads it from package.json at build, so
#     the release shown always matches CHANGELOG.md.
